## Worker-07 final report — cosmic-censorship swarm

**Status:** assigned work delivered; **14 schema-valid outbox events ingested**; no node `done`, no `validation_status=passed`, no gate verdict claimed. ~1.1 of 4 budgeted agent-hours; timeline in `artifacts/worker-07/CHECKPOINT.md`.

### Assignment adopted (arrived 23:19, found 23:26)
`asg-2026-09-11-L0-deepseek-flash-07-16` — node **L0**, artifact `ledger/theorems.jsonl`, gate **G-LIT**. I checked the inbox at 23:16–23:20 (empty), so the no-assignment branch ran first; once the card was found, L0 took priority.

**L0 delivery:** 7 source records + 15 theorem rows (9 accepted / 4 provisional / 2 unresolved) into new `batch-w07.jsonl` files, then materialized the canonical ledger with the literature lead's builder. Five sources verified by arXiv abstract fetches; Penrose 1969 and Choptuik 1993 stayed honestly `unresolved`. Caught and discarded a fabricated ID: `1501.04593` is an unrelated holography paper — Luk–Oh is `1501.04598`.

**Incident (blocker filed):** the lead's 23:27 directory rewrite **deleted my injected batches**; the rebuilt ledger had zero W07 rows. Durable generator/batches are preserved under `artifacts/worker-07/`, the generator now defaults to no-inject, and a `blocker` event asks for an append-only or merge-tool contract. On re-inspection all 15 rows had equal-or-stronger canonical equivalents (D-001, T-101, T-103, T-201, T-206, T-208, T-209), so I **did not re-inject duplicates**; an annotated supersession map records why.

### Durable verification contribution
- **Quote grounding** (`check_grounding.py`): all 30 declared quotes in my 13 grounded rows match their sources verbatim; **34 of 43 accepted lead rows declare no grounding** — a checkability gap for L1, not proof of error.
- **Duplication triage** (`check_duplication.py`, canonical work keys, tiered): 10 actionable pairs in 5 clusters, 23 review-tier, 0 duplicate source records.
- **Class-separation falsification harness** (pre-assignment proposal W07-01): the shared gate caught only 3/17 genuine class-merge fixtures on `c4769b99ab70` and `bb0522e94148`, with 1/10 legitimate controls falsely flagged. On `6873cb512431` it detects **17/17 and accepts 10/10 — the fix landed**, and the lead adopted the corpus as `runtime/bin/classsep_regression.py` (PASS). I therefore **retracted the counterexample claim for the current revision** (`w07-status-A1-fix-confirmed`), per the falsifier I had stated; it remains true only for the two pinned, snapshotted revisions.

